{
  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "The strongest result (config_001: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat → 0.688) came from multiprofile + transformer aggregation, but we cannot yet attribute the gain to the image modality vs. the RNA multiprofile signal alone. Image-only performance is very weak (0.208), and in singleprofile the image adds only ~1.6% over RNA alone (0.536 vs 0.520). config_049 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) is a clean single-variable ablation of config_001 that isolates whether the image contributes meaningfully in the multiprofile+transformer regime. If rna_only+multiprofile+transformer approaches 0.688, the image is redundant and we should focus budget on RNA encoder variants (scgpt, pca_n2000); if it is substantially lower, the image provides complementary signal and we should explore image encoder and fusion choices. This resolves the single most important uncertainty for directing all subsequent experiments under the limited budget."
}

